<Application
    x:Class="CrypticRealm.Probe.App"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!-- Deliberately NO XamlControlsResources.

         The crash dump from a real Xbox Series X shows STATUS_STOWED_EXCEPTION
         (0xC000027B) thrown inside Windows.UI.Xaml.dll during startup, in a
         probe whose entire UI is one TextBlock. The frameworks resolved
         (Microsoft.UI.Xaml.dll is loaded in the dump), so this is not a missing
         dependency: something in XAML initialisation throws and nothing catches
         it.

         The WinUI 2 resource dictionary is the only thing this probe pulls from
         WinUI, and it uses no WinUI controls, so dropping it isolates whether
         loading those resources is what throws. -->
</Application>
